WEBVTT

00:00:01.245 --> 00:00:22.104
Money for a Motorbike by John Milne It was the month of June and the weather was beautiful.

00:00:22.164 --> 00:00:24.426
Stuart left school.

00:00:24.486 --> 00:00:28.037
He was on holiday but he was not happy.

00:00:28.097 --> 00:00:30.760
He did not have a motorbike.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.844
Stuart was 17 years old.

00:00:33.904 --> 00:00:37.938
He left school, but he did not start work.

00:00:37.998 --> 00:00:43.571
All his mates started work immediately, but Stuart did not want to work.

00:00:43.631 --> 00:00:48.224
He wanted a long holiday, and he needed a motorbike.

00:00:48.284 --> 00:00:53.207
Stuart lived in Leeds, a big city in the north of England.

00:00:53.268 --> 00:00:58.040
Leeds is a busy city, full of offices, shops and factories.

00:00:58.101 --> 00:01:01.094
It's not a good place for a holiday.

00:01:01.154 --> 00:01:05.407
Martin, a friend of Stuart's, worked in a garage.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:07.878
Martin had a bike for sale.

00:01:07.938 --> 00:01:11.980
It was a beauty, a Japanese Suzuki.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:18.444
Martin wanted £350 for the bike, but Stuart did not have £350.

00:01:18.504 --> 00:01:21.186
He didn't have any money.

00:01:21.246 --> 00:01:24.908
Stuart went and looked at the bike every day.

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.939
It was a beauty.

00:01:26.999 --> 00:01:29.274
He wanted to buy it.

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:33.358
Where can I find 350 pounds?

00:01:33.418 --> 00:01:36.200
Stuart asked himself.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:40.222
Stuart left the garage and walked back home.

00:01:40.282 --> 00:01:44.143
His house was in Blenham Street, near the university.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:48.115
There were lots of old empty houses in Blenham Street.

00:01:48.175 --> 00:01:51.976
The university was one of the biggest in England.

00:01:52.036 --> 00:01:55.848
The university often bought land and buildings.

00:01:55.908 --> 00:02:00.694
Most of the old houses in Blenham Street belong to the university.

00:02:00.754 --> 00:02:04.580
Some of these houses had been empty for years.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.292
Stewart often searched through them.

00:02:07.352 --> 00:02:11.546
Sometimes he found old books and gramophone records.

00:02:11.606 --> 00:02:17.652
One day, he told himself, I'll find something valuable.

00:02:17.712 --> 00:02:22.036
There was a large house at the corner of Blenheim Street.

00:02:22.096 --> 00:02:26.900
Its owner, a rich old woman, had died a few days ago.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.304
The university bought the house immediately.

00:02:30.364 --> 00:02:32.645
Now the house was empty.

00:02:32.705 --> 00:02:37.426
There was wood across the front door and the windows were broken.

00:02:37.486 --> 00:02:40.557
Someone looked out of a window.

00:02:40.617 --> 00:02:43.198
It was a man of about twenty.

00:02:43.258 --> 00:02:46.538
He had long hair and was wearing a headband.

00:02:46.598 --> 00:02:48.839
He looked strange.

00:02:48.899 --> 00:02:51.189
He was a squatter.

00:02:51.249 --> 00:02:56.520
Squatters live in old empty houses and they don't pay any rent.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.399
The stranger waved to Stuart.

00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:02.028
He wanted to speak to Stuart.

00:03:02.088 --> 00:03:04.168
What does he want?

00:03:04.228 --> 00:03:07.488
Stuart asked himself.

00:03:07.548 --> 00:03:10.350
Hi.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.000
Hello.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.001
Like to help me.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.621
Okay.

00:03:15.681 --> 00:03:17.922
Watch this house.

00:03:17.982 --> 00:03:19.702
How long?

00:03:19.762 --> 00:03:21.572
Half an hour.

00:03:21.632 --> 00:03:23.293
Okay.

00:03:23.353 --> 00:03:24.923
I'm Stuart.

00:03:24.983 --> 00:03:26.774
My name's Frank.

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:29.116
I'll go and get my things.

00:03:29.176 --> 00:03:31.450
Are you going to squat here, Frank?

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:32.652
Yes.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:35.004
Don't let anyone else in.

00:03:35.064 --> 00:03:37.136
I'll be back soon.

00:03:37.196 --> 00:03:38.586
OK.

00:03:38.646 --> 00:03:41.308
See you.

00:03:41.368 --> 00:03:45.853
Frank walked off slowly down the street.

00:03:45.912 --> 00:03:50.286
His head was bent forward, and he was looking down at the pavement.

00:03:50.346 --> 00:03:54.130
He was about 20, but he looked much older.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:58.925
Frank went round the corner and Stewart turned towards the house.

00:03:58.985 --> 00:04:01.138
It looked interesting.

00:04:01.198 --> 00:04:04.960
The window was low, quite near the ground.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.112
The street was empty.

00:04:07.171 --> 00:04:12.134
Stuart put one leg over the window sill and looked inside.

00:04:12.194 --> 00:04:15.556
Outside the sun was shining brightly.

00:04:15.616 --> 00:04:18.968
Inside the house it was dark.

00:04:19.028 --> 00:04:22.330
Stuart stood for a few moments and waited.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:26.102
Slowly the inside of the room became clearer.

00:04:26.162 --> 00:04:28.768
There was a calendar on the wall.

00:04:28.828 --> 00:04:32.804
Lots of old newspapers were lying around on the floor.

00:04:32.864 --> 00:04:36.036
There was a mattress against the far wall.

00:04:36.096 --> 00:04:38.068
It looked new.

00:04:38.128 --> 00:04:41.270
Stuart looked up and down the street.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.462
There was no one around.

00:04:43.522 --> 00:04:47.654
He quickly climbed into the room.

00:04:47.714 --> 00:04:53.658
Stuart walked to the middle of the room and kicked away the old newspapers.

00:04:53.718 --> 00:04:55.888
There was nothing underneath them.

00:04:55.948 --> 00:05:00.678
There was no carpet, and the floorboards were covered with dirt.

00:05:00.738 --> 00:05:04.230
Stuart took the calendar down from the wall.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.382
It was an old one, five years old.

00:05:07.442 --> 00:05:10.574
No one had changed it for five years.

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:12.986
Then Stuart remembered.

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:17.678
The owner of the house, the old woman, had been ill for a long time.

00:05:17.738 --> 00:05:21.881
She hadn't got out of her bed for five years.

00:05:21.941 --> 00:05:25.729
The mattress was leaning against the far wall.

00:05:25.789 --> 00:05:29.146
Stuart went over and looked at it carefully.

00:05:29.206 --> 00:05:31.696
It was a good mattress.

00:05:31.756 --> 00:05:36.598
Stuart picked up the mattress and turned it over carefully.

00:05:36.658 --> 00:05:42.420
There was some stitching along one side, about ten centimeters long.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:48.372
Stuart held the mattress between his knees and took out a small knife.

00:05:48.432 --> 00:05:54.066
Stuart cut the stitches carefully and then put his hand in the hole.

00:05:54.126 --> 00:05:58.870
He felt a bundle of newspapers and pulled it out.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:02.952
He quickly unwrapped it.

00:06:03.011 --> 00:06:11.154
Inside the bundle of newspapers, there were some banknotes.

00:06:11.214 --> 00:06:16.306
Suddenly Stuart heard a voice.

00:06:16.366 --> 00:06:18.306
It was Frank.

00:06:18.366 --> 00:06:20.157
Hey!

00:06:20.217 --> 00:06:21.808
Stuart!

00:06:21.867 --> 00:06:23.552
Where are you?

00:06:23.612 --> 00:06:25.606
Frank was shouting.

00:06:25.665 --> 00:06:30.748
Stuart quickly wrapped up the money inside the newspapers.

00:06:30.807 --> 00:06:35.038
He held the bundle behind his back.

00:06:35.098 --> 00:06:37.359
I'm in here, Frank!

00:06:37.419 --> 00:06:39.200
He shouted.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:43.572
Frank came up to the window and looked into the room.

00:06:43.631 --> 00:06:45.952
What are you doing in there?

00:06:46.012 --> 00:06:47.492
Frank asked.

00:06:47.552 --> 00:06:50.204
Nothing, replied Stuart.

00:06:50.263 --> 00:06:52.398
I'm looking around.

00:06:52.458 --> 00:06:56.804
Frank climbed into the room and came closer to Stuart.

00:06:56.864 --> 00:06:59.005
Stuart moved to the wall.

00:06:59.065 --> 00:07:02.768
He held the bundle of newspapers behind his back.

00:07:02.828 --> 00:07:05.709
Frank looked round the room.

00:07:05.769 --> 00:07:09.330
He didn't see Stuart's knife on the floor.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:12.282
You haven't taken anything, have you?

00:07:12.342 --> 00:07:13.984
asked Frank.

00:07:14.044 --> 00:07:18.476
I haven't taken anything of yours, replied Stuart.

00:07:18.536 --> 00:07:22.764
You've moved this mattress, said Frank.

00:07:22.824 --> 00:07:26.861
Frank picked up the mattress and turned it over carefully.

00:07:26.921 --> 00:07:30.382
Then he saw the hole in the side.

00:07:30.442 --> 00:07:33.373
You cut this mattress.

00:07:33.433 --> 00:07:35.504
It was stitched.

00:07:35.564 --> 00:07:37.814
Is this your knife?

00:07:37.874 --> 00:07:39.284
Yes.

00:07:39.344 --> 00:07:41.405
What were you doing?

00:07:41.465 --> 00:07:43.016
Nothing.

00:07:43.076 --> 00:07:45.476
You found something.

00:07:45.536 --> 00:07:47.106
I didn't.

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:49.577
What's that in your hand?

00:07:49.637 --> 00:07:51.008
Where?

00:07:51.068 --> 00:07:53.028
Behind your back.

00:07:53.088 --> 00:07:54.737
Nothing.

00:07:54.797 --> 00:07:57.098
You've got something.

00:07:57.158 --> 00:07:59.638
Some old newspapers.

00:07:59.698 --> 00:08:01.469
Hand them over.

00:08:01.529 --> 00:08:04.230
They're mine!

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.570
Stewart remembered the motorbike.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:09.210
He needed the money.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:11.021
He was going to keep it.

00:08:11.081 --> 00:08:13.911
It was his money, not Frank's.

00:08:13.971 --> 00:08:17.422
Frank was holding Stewart's knife in his hand.

00:08:17.482 --> 00:08:19.823
He came nearer to Stewart.

00:08:19.882 --> 00:08:22.805
Give me those newspapers.

00:08:22.865 --> 00:08:24.598
He said again.

00:08:24.658 --> 00:08:27.000
Stuart had an idea.

00:08:27.059 --> 00:08:30.763
There's something else in the mattress, he said to Frank.

00:08:30.823 --> 00:08:33.225
There was something under the newspapers.

00:08:33.284 --> 00:08:35.046
It's still there.

00:08:35.106 --> 00:08:38.238
Frank looked at Stuart for a few moments.

00:08:38.298 --> 00:08:40.610
He didn't believe him at first.

00:08:40.671 --> 00:08:43.872
Look and see, said Stuart.

00:08:43.932 --> 00:08:46.705
Frank put the knife down on the floor.

00:08:46.765 --> 00:08:51.182
He picked up the mattress and put his hand deep in the hole.

00:08:51.242 --> 00:08:53.917
Stuart did not wait for a moment.

00:08:53.977 --> 00:08:58.329
He turned and jumped out through the window into the street.

00:08:58.388 --> 00:09:01.079
He ran quickly.

00:09:01.139 --> 00:09:03.520
There was a turning on the right.

00:09:03.579 --> 00:09:06.020
Stuart ran round the corner.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.260
He heard a shout behind him.

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:10.081
It was Frank.

00:09:10.141 --> 00:09:14.552
Round the corner, there was another old empty house.

00:09:14.612 --> 00:09:17.542
It had a large garden on one side.

00:09:17.602 --> 00:09:20.914
Thick bushes had grown all over the garden.

00:09:20.974 --> 00:09:23.808
Stuart jumped over the low wall.

00:09:23.868 --> 00:09:28.472
He ran for a few meters and then hid under some bushes.

00:09:28.532 --> 00:09:32.094
Stuart heard more shouting and footsteps.

00:09:32.154 --> 00:09:36.568
The footsteps became louder than they stopped.

00:09:36.628 --> 00:09:39.140
Stuart waited silently.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.392
He did not breathe.

00:09:41.452 --> 00:09:44.786
Then the footsteps started once again.

00:09:44.846 --> 00:09:49.680
Stuart laughed quietly to himself.

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:54.183
Frank had quickly picked up Stuart's knife.

00:09:54.243 --> 00:09:56.964
He jumped out of the window after him.

00:09:57.024 --> 00:09:58.906
Frank saw Stuart.

00:09:58.966 --> 00:10:01.068
He was running around the corner.

00:10:01.127 --> 00:10:04.260
Frank ran after him and turned the corner.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.572
But the street was empty.

00:10:06.632 --> 00:10:10.654
Frank stopped for a few moments and looked around.

00:10:10.714 --> 00:10:13.447
He noticed the old garden.

00:10:13.507 --> 00:10:16.068
Perhaps he's in there.

00:10:16.128 --> 00:10:17.910
Thought Frank.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.878
But everything in the garden was quiet.

00:10:20.938 --> 00:10:22.936
Frank saw nothing.

00:10:22.996 --> 00:10:26.408
There was another corner farther down the street.

00:10:26.469 --> 00:10:29.180
Frank started running again.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:32.583
He was still holding Stewart's knife.

00:10:32.643 --> 00:10:34.914
Stewart was happy.

00:10:34.974 --> 00:10:37.966
He had escaped from Frank with the money.

00:10:38.026 --> 00:10:42.600
Stewart sat up under the bushes and opened up the newspapers.

00:10:42.661 --> 00:10:45.962
The banknotes were wrapped tightly together.

00:10:46.022 --> 00:10:49.993
Stewart unwrapped them and counted them carefully.

00:10:50.053 --> 00:10:51.972
10, 20, 30, 320, 325.

00:10:51.992 --> 00:11:01.399
Stuart had found 325 pounds, and Martin wanted 350 pounds for his motorbike.

00:11:01.419 --> 00:11:15.536
It was cool in the garden, and Stuart lay back under the bushes.

00:11:15.596 --> 00:11:25.387
I'll wait here for half an hour," thought Stuart.

00:11:25.447 --> 00:11:29.098
Then I'll go to Martin.

00:11:29.158 --> 00:11:32.868
It was now nearly twelve o'clock.

00:11:32.928 --> 00:11:35.039
The day was getting much hotter.

00:11:35.099 --> 00:11:38.550
A police car was parked in a side street.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.210
There were two policemen in the car.

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:45.881
The sergeant, a fat, round-faced man, was half asleep.

00:11:45.941 --> 00:11:48.672
The other policeman was younger and taller.

00:11:48.732 --> 00:11:50.548
He was a constable.

00:11:50.608 --> 00:11:53.966
Suddenly, the constable sat up.

00:11:54.026 --> 00:11:56.878
He had seen something strange.

00:11:56.938 --> 00:11:58.950
Wake up, Sergeant!

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:00.091
He shouted.

00:12:00.151 --> 00:12:01.932
Look over there!

00:12:01.993 --> 00:12:03.424
Where?

00:12:03.483 --> 00:12:04.834
What?

00:12:04.894 --> 00:12:07.916
asked the sergeant, still half asleep.

00:12:07.976 --> 00:12:09.308
Over there!

00:12:09.368 --> 00:12:11.289
Someone's running with a knife!

00:12:11.349 --> 00:12:12.990
Replied the constable.

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:14.671
The man's gone mad!

00:12:14.731 --> 00:12:16.172
It's this heat!

00:12:16.232 --> 00:12:17.203
Quick!

00:12:17.263 --> 00:12:18.934
Get out and catch him!

00:12:18.994 --> 00:12:21.014
Said the sergeant.

00:12:21.074 --> 00:12:24.554
The two policemen jumped out of their car.

00:12:24.614 --> 00:12:26.666
Frank saw the policeman.

00:12:26.726 --> 00:12:30.118
He threw Stuart's knife away and started to run.

00:12:30.178 --> 00:12:34.570
The constable soon caught him and held his arm tightly.

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:38.262
The sergeant found the knife in some long grass.

00:12:38.322 --> 00:12:41.764
The constable took Frank towards the police car.

00:12:41.824 --> 00:12:43.786
The sergeant came up to them.

00:12:43.846 --> 00:12:46.148
He was holding the knife.

00:12:46.208 --> 00:12:48.999
Oh, it's you.

00:12:49.059 --> 00:12:51.748
The sergeant said to Frank.

00:12:51.808 --> 00:12:54.686
What's going on, Frank?

00:12:54.746 --> 00:12:56.956
I'm looking for a guy.

00:12:57.016 --> 00:12:58.516
With a knife?

00:12:58.576 --> 00:13:00.327
What guy?

00:13:00.387 --> 00:13:02.558
He's stolen my money.

00:13:02.618 --> 00:13:04.248
What money?

00:13:04.308 --> 00:13:06.448
How much money?

00:13:06.508 --> 00:13:07.969
I don't know.

00:13:08.029 --> 00:13:09.139
A lot.

00:13:09.199 --> 00:13:11.310
He don't know.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:13.490
Where did you get it?

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:16.091
In an old house.

00:13:16.151 --> 00:13:24.114
Come on, into the car.

00:13:24.174 --> 00:13:31.068
Where are you taking me?"

00:13:31.128 --> 00:13:32.408
asked Frank.

00:13:32.468 --> 00:13:35.949
To the police station replied the constable.

00:13:36.009 --> 00:13:37.920
But I haven't done anything.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.430
The money was mine.

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:40.911
That guy took it.

00:13:40.971 --> 00:13:42.311
But what's his name?

00:13:42.371 --> 00:13:43.292
Stuart.

00:13:43.352 --> 00:13:44.922
Stuart took it.

00:13:44.982 --> 00:13:48.233
Ooh, Stuart asked the constable.

00:13:48.294 --> 00:13:51.724
I met him in an old house replied Frank.

00:13:51.784 --> 00:13:55.196
Where you found the money asked the sergeant.

00:13:55.256 --> 00:13:59.584
Yes, I found it inside a mattress said Frank.

00:13:59.644 --> 00:14:01.563
Who's got the money now?"

00:14:01.623 --> 00:14:02.994
asked the sergeant.

00:14:03.054 --> 00:14:06.615
That guy, Stuart, he ran away with it.

00:14:06.675 --> 00:14:13.968
So now we have to find Stuart, said the Constable.

00:14:14.028 --> 00:14:19.882
Stuart waited in the garden for half an hour.

00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:21.882
It was getting hotter.

00:14:21.942 --> 00:14:24.364
It was nearly twelve o'clock.

00:14:24.424 --> 00:14:28.184
I'll have to move now, thought Stuart.

00:14:28.244 --> 00:14:31.676
Martin goes for his lunch at half past twelve.

00:14:31.736 --> 00:14:35.058
Stuart looked out carefully from the bushes.

00:14:35.118 --> 00:14:37.171
The garden was empty.

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:40.262
He hurried out of the garden onto the street.

00:14:40.322 --> 00:14:43.044
He walked towards Martin's garage.

00:14:43.104 --> 00:14:46.288
Stuart did not see the police car.

00:14:46.348 --> 00:14:50.060
It stopped outside the garden a few moments later.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:53.852
Look in this garden, Frank told the policeman.

00:14:53.912 --> 00:14:59.417
Perhaps he's hiding in here.

00:14:59.477 --> 00:15:04.410
Hi Martin.

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:06.092
Hi Stuart.

00:15:06.152 --> 00:15:08.333
How much for the bike?

00:15:08.393 --> 00:15:08.993
£350.

00:15:09.013 --> 00:15:09.213
I want it.

00:15:09.233 --> 00:15:09.574
How much for me?

00:15:09.594 --> 00:15:10.484
Still £350.

00:15:10.544 --> 00:15:12.845
Have you any money?

00:15:12.905 --> 00:15:13.696
Yes.

00:15:13.756 --> 00:15:14.717
How much?

00:15:14.737 --> 00:15:14.917
£300.

00:15:14.957 --> 00:15:16.498
That's not enough.

00:15:16.538 --> 00:15:16.698
£325?

00:15:16.718 --> 00:15:25.465
Okay, she's yours.

00:15:25.525 --> 00:15:34.542
Great.

00:15:34.602 --> 00:15:38.364
Thanks.

00:15:38.424 --> 00:15:43.647
The policeman got out of the car.

00:15:43.706 --> 00:15:45.978
Frank got out too.

00:15:46.038 --> 00:15:48.939
The Constable held his arm tightly.

00:15:48.999 --> 00:15:51.510
The sergeant went into the garden.

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:53.831
He looked around for some time.

00:15:53.891 --> 00:15:55.612
Then he came back.

00:15:55.672 --> 00:15:58.786
He was holding a bundle of newspapers.

00:15:58.846 --> 00:16:04.852
There's no one there," the sergeant said, but I found these old newspapers.

00:16:04.912 --> 00:16:06.393
That's them!

00:16:06.453 --> 00:16:07.514
Shouted Frank.

00:16:07.574 --> 00:16:10.476
Something was wrapped in those newspapers.

00:16:10.536 --> 00:16:14.528
Just then a motorbike drove up towards the police car.

00:16:14.588 --> 00:16:16.010
That's him!

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:17.971
Shouted Frank excitedly.

00:16:18.031 --> 00:16:19.542
That's the guy!

00:16:19.602 --> 00:16:22.604
He's bought a motorbike with my money.

00:16:22.664 --> 00:16:24.105
Stop!

00:16:24.165 --> 00:16:26.216
The sergeant called us to it.

00:16:26.276 --> 00:16:29.176
Stop!

00:16:29.236 --> 00:16:33.517
Stewart did not see Frank.

00:16:33.576 --> 00:16:35.798
What do the police want?

00:16:35.858 --> 00:16:37.780
Stewart asked himself.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:39.902
I haven't done anything wrong.

00:16:39.962 --> 00:16:42.224
I'm driving correctly.

00:16:42.284 --> 00:16:45.676
Stewart stopped the bike by the side of the road.

00:16:45.736 --> 00:16:47.918
He took off his helmet.

00:16:47.978 --> 00:16:50.120
Is that bike yours?

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:51.882
The sergeant asked him.

00:16:51.942 --> 00:16:53.913
Yes, it's mine.

00:16:53.973 --> 00:16:55.354
replied Stewart.

00:16:55.414 --> 00:16:58.176
I bought it at the garage down the road.

00:16:58.236 --> 00:17:01.031
Then Stewart saw Frank.

00:17:01.091 --> 00:17:03.685
What have you told these cops?

00:17:03.745 --> 00:17:06.836
Stuart shouted angrily at Frank.

00:17:06.897 --> 00:17:12.029
We'll all go to this garage, said the sergeant.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:17.382
They all walked back to Martin's garage.

00:17:17.443 --> 00:17:22.726
A big black cloud now covered the sun.

00:17:22.786 --> 00:17:24.936
It was beginning to rain.

00:17:24.996 --> 00:17:30.220
So, this loud fades you 325 pounds for this bike.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:33.152
The sergeant said to Martin.

00:17:33.212 --> 00:17:35.014
Martin agreed.

00:17:35.074 --> 00:17:37.376
And where did you get this money?

00:17:37.436 --> 00:17:39.588
The sergeant asked Stuart.

00:17:39.648 --> 00:17:41.260
I found it.

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:42.451
Replied Stuart.

00:17:42.511 --> 00:17:44.102
I found it in a mattress.

00:17:44.162 --> 00:17:46.424
It was in an empty house.

00:17:46.484 --> 00:17:49.697
The sergeant took the money from Martin.

00:17:49.757 --> 00:17:52.880
We'll look after this money, he said.

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:54.832
You two can go now.

00:17:54.892 --> 00:17:56.663
It's my money!

00:17:56.723 --> 00:17:58.228
Shouted Frank.

00:17:58.288 --> 00:18:01.692
Do you want to come to the police station with us?"

00:18:01.752 --> 00:18:03.803
asked the constable.

00:18:03.863 --> 00:18:07.834
Frank walked away, still shouting.

00:18:07.894 --> 00:18:11.556
I'm sorry, Martin said to Stuart.

00:18:11.616 --> 00:18:13.437
It's my bike again.

00:18:13.497 --> 00:18:16.868
Not for long, replied Stuart.

00:18:16.928 --> 00:18:18.829
What do you mean?

00:18:18.889 --> 00:18:20.900
Asked the sergeant.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:25.352
It has started to rain now, replied Stuart.

00:18:25.412 --> 00:18:27.388
I don't want a holiday.

00:18:27.448 --> 00:18:29.484
I'm going to get a job.

00:18:29.544 --> 00:18:44.980
I'm going to save another 325 pounds and buy that bike.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:19:06.305
Money for a Motorbike was read by William Gaminara and the recording produced by James Richardson at StudioAVP London.

